# Evidence reading quality

Ground each conclusion in the cited original material, with enough context to answer the question at the requested level of detail. Keep claims tied to the Source and version actually read, and preserve relevant conditions, uncertainty and disagreements when writing Notes.

Use retained acquisition metadata alongside document text when checking identity, dates and discovery scope. Preserve each field's stated meaning and provenance: creation, update and publication dates are different facts. A missing statement in the document does not establish that the supplied metadata lacks it; check the relevant files before reporting absence. Keep supported findings and report any unresolved qualification separately.

Distinguish information not yet checked from information the Source does not provide. When combining Sources, verify that their evidence supports the connection. Stay within the assigned Source scope; local findings do not establish global coverage.
